# Supply-chain hardening: when resolving dependencies, refuse any version
# published fewer than this many days ago. Most malicious package releases are
# detected and unpublished within hours-to-days, so this cooldown means a
# compromised version is very likely caught and yanked before this repo ever
# resolves it into the lockfile.
#
# Scope: applies when npm builds the dependency tree (`npm install`, `npm update`,
# adding a dep). `npm ci` reproduces the committed lockfile as-is, so the gate's
# value is keeping a too-new version out of the lockfile in the first place.
#
# Requires npm >= 11.10.0 (the `min-release-age` config; value is in days).
# Older npm clients silently ignore this line, so it is safe for all contributors.
# To bypass for a single urgent install (e.g. a security fix): npm i pkg --min-release-age=0
min-release-age=7
